{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>They went out, standing.</b> With posture erect — to defy and to blaspheme, as in ״וַיִּתְיַצֵּב אַרְבָּעִים יוֹם״ (1 Samuel 17) of Goliath (Tanchuma)." "<b>And their wives, and their children, and their little ones.</b> Come and see how severe is strife — for a court below does not punish until he has produced two hairs, and a court above until twenty years, yet here even nursing infants perished (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:20.047189424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}